# Code used for complex non-orthogonal building handling; generating conformal geometry and applying it the the application of mesh generation
This directory contains a part of the code used in following publication:

Ezendam, T., van der, Hofmeyer, H., van der Wal, S., Perevendieva K.G., and Emmerich, M. T. M. "Handling Complex Building Geometries for Disciplinary Processing in Conceptual Building Design Simulation and Optimization". In: Computing in Civil Engineering (2026). DOI: 10.1061/JCCEE5.CPENG-6922 

In this publication, three methods to handle complex geometry were tested and compared. 
In this directory, all the code and obtained data for the Triangular Partitioning (TP) method can be found. 
The remaining code and data for the other two methods can be found at:
    - Tying method convergence study source code and data: 
      Ezendam, T., van der Wal, S., & Hofmeyer, H. (2026). BSO Toolbox: Tying method (Version 1.0.0) [Computer software]. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23476925
    - Iterative Partitioning (IP) method convergence study source code and data: 
      Ezendam, T., & Hofmeyer, H. BSO Toolbox (Version 1.0.0) [Computer software]. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23477078

The following code and data is included in this directory:

* an executable to test the IP and TP method on their effectiveness of generating a conformal geometry (~/Complex_NOBSD_handeling/Effectiveness_conformal_making)
* an executable to compare the mesh quality of the IP and TP method to a benchmark case and a mesh quality test for a set of Non-orthogonal designs (~/Complex_NOBSD_handling/Mesh_Quality_study_IP_TP_methods)
* an executable to perform a mesh convergenge study for the TP method and the data files and reference to the source code for the IP and Tying method (~/Complex_NOBSD_handling//Mesh_convergence_study_IP_TP_Tying_methods_Rectangular_BSO)
* All the 20 non-orthogonal building designs where the IP and TP methods has been tested on for making conformal geometry and in the mesh convergence study (~/Complex_NOBSD_handling/Non_orthogonal_designs)
